    <item>
      <title>Infringements Allegedly Occurred in Delhi, Not WB: Calcutta HC Dismisses Kuwait Based Company’s Challenge to DGTR ADD Findings [Read Order]</title>
      <link>https://www.taxscan.in/top-stories/infringements-allegedly-occurred-in-delhi-not-wb-calcutta-hc-dismisses-kuwait-based-companys-challenge-to-dgtr-add-findings-1440662</link>
      <description>The Court drew a clear distinction between “cause of action” and mere “consequential injury.” The judge held that an apprehended adverse effect on business in West Bengal does not amount to a legally relevant part of the cause of action for challenging the DGTR’s findings.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.taxscan.in/top-stories/infringements-allegedly-occurred-in-delhi-not-wb-calcutta-hc-dismisses-kuwait-based-companys-challenge-to-dgtr-add-findings-1440662</guid>
